---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"

const html =
  "<p>KoAkademy ships four developer observability tools. They live <strong>outside</strong> the Filament panel and the admin workspace, each on its own path. When enabled and permitted, they appear in the admin panel sidebar under the <strong>Observability</strong> group (each opens in a new tab).</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Tool</th>\n<th>Default path</th>\n<th>Who can open it</th>\n<th>Enable flag</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Laralyze</td>\n<td><code>/laralyze</code></td>\n<td>Primary role <strong>or</strong> Spatie role <code>developer</code> / <code>super_admin</code></td>\n<td><code>LARALYZE_ENABLED</code> (default on)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pulse</td>\n<td><code>/pulse</code></td>\n<td>Spatie role <code>super_admin</code> (or the configured admin e-mail)</td>\n<td><code>PULSE_ENABLED</code> (default off in <code>.env.example</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Telescope</td>\n<td><code>/telescope</code></td>\n<td>Spatie role <code>developer</code></td>\n<td><code>TELESCOPE_ENABLED</code> (default off in <code>.env.example</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Horizon</td>\n<td><code>/horizon</code></td>\n<td>Primary role <code>super_admin</code> or Spatie role <code>super_admin</code></td>\n<td>Installed only in the production Docker images</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Paths for Laralyze, Pulse, and Telescope are configurable (<code>laralyze.path</code>, <code>pulse.path</code>, <code>telescope.path</code>). Horizon is only registered when the package is present — see <code>bootstrap/providers.php</code>.</p>\n<h2>Laralyze</h2>\n<p>Self-hosted production monitoring (requests, jobs, queries, exceptions, cache, AI calls, logs, users, visits). Installed via <code>mohammed-mojaly/laralyze</code>; config at <code>config/laralyze.php</code>, tables <code>laralyze_*</code>.</p>\n<p>Access is decided by the <code>viewLaralyze</code> gate (<code>app/Providers/AppServiceProvider.php</code>, enforced first in <code>app/Providers/AuthServiceProvider.php</code>):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>primary <code>users.role</code> is <code>developer</code> or <code>super_admin</code>, <strong>or</strong></li>\n<li>Spatie role is <code>developer</code> or <code>super_admin</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Guests and all other roles get <strong>403</strong>. The account&#39;s Spatie roles are managed on the Users edit page (<code>role</code> is the primary column, <code>roles[]</code> are Spatie roles) — a user with primary <code>admin</code> but Spatie <code>super_admin</code> <strong>is</strong> allowed.</p>\n<p>Production notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Run <code>php artisan migrate --force</code> after deploy (Laralyze tables are pending until then), then <code>php artisan optimize</code> and <code>php artisan queue:restart</code>.</li>\n<li>The scheduler must run every minute (Laralyze trim/digest/server tasks). The Docker images already run it via Supercronic.</li>\n<li>Ask AI (<code>LARALYZE_ASSISTANT_ENABLED</code>) is <strong>off by default</strong> because it can send recorded context and readable application code to the configured AI provider. Tests force <code>LARALYZE_ENABLED=false</code> (<code>phpunit.xml</code>).</li>\n<li>Log in on the <strong>admin host</strong> (<code>ADMIN_HOST</code>, e.g. <code>admin.dccp.edu.ph</code>) and open <code>/laralyze</code> on that same host. Session cookies are host-only (<code>SESSION_DOMAIN</code> unset), so a session from the portal host is not sent to the admin host and vice versa.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Pulse</h2>\n<p>Request/queue/cache performance dashboard. Gate <code>viewPulse</code> (<code>app/Providers/PulseServiceProvider.php</code>) allows the configured admin e-mail or Spatie <code>super_admin</code>. Disabled by default for a minimal local setup (<code>TELESCOPE_ENABLED=false</code>, <code>PULSE_ENABLED=false</code> in <code>.env.example</code>).</p>\n<h2>Telescope</h2>\n<p>Debug assistant for exceptions, failed requests/jobs, and scheduled tasks. Gate <code>viewTelescope</code> (<code>app/Providers/TelescopeServiceProvider.php</code>) allows Spatie role <code>developer</code>. Outside <code>local</code>, Telescope records only reportable exceptions, failed requests/jobs, scheduled tasks, and monitored tags, and hides <code>_token</code> plus cookie/auth headers.</p>\n<h2>Horizon</h2>\n<p>Redis queue dashboard. Only installed in the production Docker images and only registered when the package exists. Gate <code>viewHorizon</code> (<code>app/Providers/AuthServiceProvider.php</code>) allows primary <code>super_admin</code> or Spatie <code>super_admin</code>.</p>\n<h2>Logs &amp; retention</h2>\n<p><strong>System Management → Logs &amp; Retention</strong> (<code>View:SystemManagementLogRetention</code>, <code>Update:SystemManagementLogRetention</code>) purges or schedules cleanup of what those tools record.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Source</th>\n<th>Tables / model</th>\n<th>Deleted by cleanup</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Pulse</td>\n<td><code>pulse_entries</code>, <code>pulse_values</code>, <code>pulse_aggregates</code></td>\n<td>Records older than the retention period, or all of them on purge</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Telescope</td>\n<td><code>telescope_entries</code> (tags cascade)</td>\n<td>Entries older than the retention period, or all of them on purge</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mail</td>\n<td>the configured mail model plus its events, attachments, and mailables</td>\n<td>Logged messages older than the retention period, or all of them on purge — with their stored attachment files</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Activity</td>\n<td>the configured activity model</td>\n<td>Audit records older than the retention period, or all of them on purge</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>What cleanup deliberately leaves alone:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Students, enrollments, finance, and every other school record.</li>\n<li>Mail records with an <strong>unsuppressed</strong> hard bounce, complaint, or unsubscribe — the suppression list keeps working after a purge.</li>\n<li>Telescope <strong>monitored tags</strong> (<code>telescope_monitoring</code>); only the entries and their per-entry tags go.</li>\n<li>Activity records under the <code>system-log-maintenance</code> log name, which hold the cleanup audit trail.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Behavior worth knowing:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Deletion is instance-wide. A purge affects every school, so the page says so before you confirm.</li>\n<li>Each action requires typing <code>PRUNE</code> or <code>PURGE</code>. Cleanup runs on the queue in bounded batches (<code>CleanSystemLogs</code>), continues in a fresh job for large sources, and is serialized per source by both a queue lock and the overlap middleware. A second request for a source that already has a queued or running cleanup is rejected.</li>\n<li>A run snapshots the highest primary key per table when it is queued, so records written <em>after</em> you confirm are never deleted by that run.</li>\n<li>Recording is never switched off by cleanup. Pulse, Telescope, and the mail and activity loggers keep collecting, and dashboards fill with fresh data immediately. Pulse also keeps its own <code>PULSE_STORAGE_KEEP</code> trim, which is independent of the schedule here.</li>\n<li>Sources whose storage is not usable (non-database Pulse/Telescope driver, missing tables, unreadable connection) are reported as <strong>Storage not configured</strong> or <strong>Storage unavailable</strong> with a Retry action; the rest of the page still loads, and cleanup for that source is refused instead of silently doing nothing.</li>\n<li>Schedule fields are read from <code>general_settings.more_configs[&#39;log_retention&#39;]</code> on every scheduler tick, so saving a schedule needs no deploy and no container restart.</li>\n<li>Defaults match the package configuration: Pulse 7 days, Telescope 1 day (enabled in production, which preserves the previous daily <code>telescope:prune --hours=24</code> behavior), Mail 30 days (<code>mails.database.pruning.after</code>), Activity 365 days (<code>activitylog.delete_records_older_than_days</code>). The other schedules start disabled.</li>\n<li><code>php artisan system-logs:prune-due</code> runs every minute via <code>onOneServer()</code> and queues each due source at most once per minute. Cleanup needs the scheduler <strong>and</strong> a queue worker; a worker that is not running leaves runs queued and visible in <strong>Cleanup history</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Deploy notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Run <code>php artisan migrate --force</code>. Two migrations are involved: <code>log_cleanup_runs</code> (run history) and the permission grant for the new section. Without them the page loads with a <strong>Migration required</strong> notice and cleanup stays disabled.</li>\n<li>After changing this area&#39;s code, run <code>php artisan optimize:clear</code> and reload Octane / restart the container, since gates and policies are held in worker memory.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Troubleshooting 403</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Role mismatch</strong> — check both sources: <code>users.role</code> column and Spatie <code>model_has_roles</code>. In <code>tinker</code>: <code>Gate::forUser($u)-&gt;allows(&#39;viewLaralyze&#39;)</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Wrong host / guard</strong> — Laralyze uses the <code>web</code> guard (staff <code>User</code>, not portal <code>Account</code>) with no <code>auth</code> redirect, so a missing session shows as 403. Use the admin host you logged in on.</li>\n<li><strong>Stale workers</strong> — FrankenPHP Octane keeps gates in memory. After deploy: <code>php artisan optimize:clear</code>, reload Octane / restart the container, and confirm <code>php artisan about</code> shows Laralyze <code>ENABLED</code> with health <code>OK</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n"
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Observability"
  path="/docs/system/observability"
  description="Developer observability tools in KoAkademy — Laralyze, Pulse, Telescope, and Horizon access, roles, enable flags, plus log purge and retention scheduling."
>
  <Fragment set:html={html} />
</DocsLayout>
